BEGIN:VEVENT
ORGANIZER;CN="Molina, Javier (NCMI, Clayton)":mailto:Javier.Molina@csiro.au
DESCRIPTION:Join the Living Atlases Information Session\n\nLiving Atlas in 
 Brazil\n\n                              \n\n\n\nWhat to expect\nThis infor
 mation session is about upporting ecologicaldata management and improving 
 Living Atlas infrastructure\nIt will range  from sampling events and quali
 ty data workflows to simplified deployment\, localization and maintenance.
 \n\nPart 1: Supporting Ecological Data Management - Clara Baringo Fonseca\
 nThis presentation looks at tools\, templates\, and workflows to organize\
 , standardize\, validate\, and publish ecological data. It will also addre
 ss current challenges and opportunities for improving data indexing\, inte
 gration\, and visualization within the Living Atlas infrastructure.\nPart 
 2: Improving Living Atlas Infrastructure - Fernando José Belmonte dos San
 tos\nThis presentation explores improvements to Living Atlas modules throu
 gh translation\, localization\, and simpler installation and updates. It w
 ill highlight DevOps practices for automating deployment and maintenance p
 rocesses\, drawing on Brazil’s experience. It will share challenges and 
 opportunities for developing reusable solutions for the wider Living Atlas
 es community.\nAbout the presenters\nFernando Jose Belmonte dos Santos is 
 a DevOps Engineer who has been working with SiBBr (Brazilian Biodiversity 
 Information System) since 2019. He contributes to the development and mode
 rnization of the platform\, focusing on the installation\, integration\, a
 daptation\, and maintenance of Living Atlases tools and infrastructure. Hi
 s work covers a wide range of technical areas\, including taxonomic servic
 es\, system security\, infrastructure management\, troubleshooting\, and t
 he overall operation and continuous improvement of SiBBr. He also supports
  the wider Living Atlases community by sharing his technical expertise and
  contributing to collaborative solutions.\nClara Baringo Fonseca is a biol
 ogist and Biodiversity Data Manager at SiBBr (Brazilian Biodiversity Infor
 mation System). She is also a member of the GBIF Brazil team and the OBIS 
 Brazil Node. She specializes in biodiversity data mobilization\, standardi
 zation\, management\, and publication\, as well as delivering training and
  capacity-building activities. Her work also focuses on data governance\, 
 data sovereignty\, and promoting best practices for biodiversity data shar
 ing and reuse.\n\n\nTime and date\nTuesday 24 Nov 2026 10-11am AEDT\n(Mond
 ay 23 Nov 11pm-12am UTC)\n\nSee it in your local time zone<https://www.tim
 eanddate.com/worldclock/fixedtime.html?msg=Living+Atlases+Information+Sess
 ion+-+Living+Atlas+in+Brazil&iso=20261124T10&p1=152&ah=1>.\n\nHow to join\
 nThis is an online event that will be broadcast using MS Teams\, follow th
 e links at the end of this meeting invitation.\n\nFurther information\nThi
 s event will be recorded and the recording made available through the Livi
 ng Atlases slack channel<https://living-atlases.gbif.org/contact> in the w
 eek after the event.\nIf you have any questions\, please reach out to supp
 ort@ala.org.au<mailto:support@ala.org.au>\n\n\n\n\n\n_____________________
